# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — WARP-243 image-vuln baseline (fixable HIGH/CRITICAL only).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (the "no flake-blocking" contract, cluster-E spec):
# docker-build.yml scans every built image with Trivy and BLOCKS on any fixable
# HIGH/CRITICAL. On a *rolling* Trivy DB that gate is non-deterministic: the
# same image + same code goes red the day the DB publishes a CVE for an
# already-installed package (Debian point-release lag on libcap2/libgnutls30,
# new npm/pip/Go advisories for pinned deps, new CVEs in bundled release
# binaries like cosign). That churn is PRE-EXISTING findings, which must never
# block a PR. Determinism comes from two mechanisms:
#
#   1. The Trivy DB is PINNED by digest in .github/trivy-db-version, so a given
#      commit always scans the same snapshot — no silent day-to-day drift.
#   2. This file lists EVERY fixable HIGH/CRITICAL present at that snapshot.
#      The trivy-action's `trivyignores` makes the gate fail ONLY on a fixable
#      finding NOT listed here — i.e. one a PR introduces, or one a deliberate
#      DB-pin bump newly surfaces. `ignore-unfixed` drops un-patchable base
#      CVEs on top. A new fixable HIGH/CRITICAL therefore still fails the build
#      (proof: tests/probe/trivy-newcve.md).
#
# HOW IT WAS GENERATED: every CI image was built + scanned against the pinned
# DB (sha256:a8a1af880ecae3a9e4fe74c0351c921b33bc083ed439ff25c9aaac0aa5d6945a)
# with `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed --scanners vuln`;
# entries are the union of fixable IDs (both build arches — some findings live
# in arch-specific prebuilt Go binaries), grouped by package with fix version.
# The first CI run is authoritative for the amd64 image set; reconcile any
# additional amd64-only IDs it surfaces into this file. Regenerate the same way
# after any DB-pin bump.
#
# BURN-DOWN (decision D3): real fixable vulns in base images + third-party
# deps/binaries — retire entries as Dependabot upgrades land (npm/pip/Go
# modules), as the Debian base picks up point-releases (libcap2/libgnutls30/
# libssl3), and as bundled Go release binaries are rebuilt (stdlib, x/crypto,
# grpc, otel, sigstore in cosign/syft). Owner: Romain.
#
# Snapshot: 2026-07-05.  Total: 89 entries.
# =============================================================================

